Did she leave any written instructions?

487
00:30:33.248 --> 00:30:34.290
No. just the tapes.

488
00:30:34.374 --> 00:30:35.542
So when you stated earlier

489
00:30:36.417 --> 00:30:38.878
that Hannah blamed the people
she named on the tapes

490
00:30:38.962 --> 00:30:40.129
and wanted them to suffer.

491
00:30:40.213 --> 00:30:42.107
you were making an assumption.
isn't that correct?

492
00:30:42.131 --> 00:30:44.259
I don't think I was making
an assumption that...

493
00:30:45.593 --> 00:30:46.593
[Tony] Mrs. Baker...

494
00:30:48.888 --> 00:30:50.849
Hannah asked me to keep secrets for her.

495
00:30:52.892 --> 00:30:53.892
I wanted to honor that.

496
00:30:57.188 --> 00:30:59.274
Yes. I was.
Yeah. I was making an assumption.

497
00:30:59.357 --> 00:31:01.293
An assumption not based
on your knowledge of Hannah

498
00:31:01.317 --> 00:31:03.027
or her intentions. isn't that correct?

499
00:31:05.572 --> 00:31:06.573
- Yes.
- And isn't it true

500
00:31:06.656 --> 00:31:08.776
that there's no particular reason
why Hannah chose you

501
00:31:08.825 --> 00:31:10.368
- to receive those tapes?
- Yes.

502
00:31:10.451 --> 00:31:13.580
So isn't it true you have no way
of knowing why Hannah left those tapes?

503
00:31:17.083 --> 00:31:18.083
Yes.

504
00:31:30.680 --> 00:31:31.680
We're brothers.

505
00:31:33.516 --> 00:31:36.227
All of us. I mean. we're fucking family.

506
00:31:38.354 --> 00:31:41.900
There's been... there's been a lot of shit
thrown our way recently.

507
00:31:41.983 --> 00:31:44.569
There are a lot of people
who are trying to tear us apart.

508
00:31:44.652 --> 00:31:46.321
but family stays together.

509
00:31:47.864 --> 00:31:49.908
Look. you guys. they can burn our field.

510
00:31:49.991 --> 00:31:52.368
but they can't change the ground
beneath it.

511
00:31:52.869 --> 00:31:54.537
That ground out there is sacred.

512
00:31:54.787 --> 00:31:56.998
That ground is where we make our stand.

513
00:31:57.248 --> 00:32:00.710
The world is divided between people
who get that and the people who don't.

514
00:32:02.003 --> 00:32:03.463
And I also just want to say that

515
00:32:03.546 --> 00:32:06.186
I'm proud to be sharing the field
with each and every one of you...

516
00:32:07.592 --> 00:32:08.801
because we're all fighters.

517
00:32:08.885 --> 00:32:11.179
We're winners. And we stand together.

518
00:32:11.679 --> 00:32:12.972
I fucking love you guys.

519
00:32:13.056 --> 00:32:15.725
- Aww!
- We love you. too. Brycey!

520
00:32:15.934 --> 00:32:17.185
All right. all right.

521
00:32:17.268 --> 00:32:20.063
Let's get out there
and let's fucking do this!

522
00:32:20.438 --> 00:32:21.898
[cheering]

523
00:32:41.167 --> 00:32:42.752
[man] Strike him out. Bryce! Let's go!

524
00:32:43.211 --> 00:32:44.295
[woman] Come on. Bryce!

525
00:32:47.340 --> 00:32:48.633
[umpire] Strike three!

526
00:32:48.716 --> 00:32:49.801
[fans cheering]

527
00:32:51.719 --> 00:32:54.013
[Tony] I can't explain how she was feeling

528
00:32:54.097 --> 00:32:56.015
or what exactly she was trying to say.

529
00:32:57.850 --> 00:33:00.019
But even if I can't say
how she was feeling.

530
00:33:00.103 --> 00:33:02.689
I can still tell you
the kind of person she was.

531
00:33:04.273 --> 00:33:05.608
I can tell you she was brave

532
00:33:06.609 --> 00:33:07.609
and loyal...

533
00:33:10.446 --> 00:33:11.698
[fans whooping]

534
00:33:17.370 --> 00:33:18.370
[umpire] Strike!

535
00:33:18.413 --> 00:33:19.956
[cheering]

536
00:33:26.713 --> 00:33:30.216
[Tony] ...and always tried to do
the right thing. even when it wasn't easy.

537
00:33:30.299 --> 00:33:32.319
- I wanted the change-up.
- I wanted to throw the heat.

538
00:33:32.343 --> 00:33:34.183
- He's catching up to you.
- Not yet. he's not.

539
00:33:34.262 --> 00:33:35.582
Just give me the change-up. okay?

540
00:33:39.183 --> 00:33:40.309
[woman] Come on. guys!

541
00:33:42.145 --> 00:33:43.145
[spits]

542
00:33:54.032 --> 00:33:55.241
[umpire] Strike three!

543
00:33:55.324 --> 00:33:56.659
[cheering]

544
00:33:57.827 --> 00:33:58.827
Time!

545
00:33:58.911 --> 00:33:59.996
Time!

546
00:34:03.791 --> 00:34:06.544
- What are you doing?
- That's 5 Ks in a row with the fastball.

547
00:34:06.627 --> 00:34:08.564
- Why fuck that up?
- Why didn't you shake me off?

548
00:34:08.588 --> 00:34:10.908
[Bryce] Why don't you just catch
what I throw and be happy?

549
00:34:10.965 --> 00:34:12.985
It's when you start thinking
that shit gets fucked up.

550
00:34:13.009 --> 00:34:15.154
[Zach] You just gave a whole
fucking speech about teamwork.

551
00:34:15.178 --> 00:34:17.698
- but that was bullshit. too. wasn't it?
- Fuck is your problem?

552
00:34:17.722 --> 00:34:20.850
You're my fucking problem. We both know
that Hannah didn't lie on those tapes.

553
00:34:21.267 --> 00:34:24.479
Zach. come on. man.
We leave this stuff off the field. right?

554
00:34:25.354 --> 00:34:27.023
Sorry. Coach. I can't anymore.

555
00:34:28.107 --> 00:34:30.276
Dempsey. Dempsey. come on!

556
00:34:30.943 --> 00:34:31.944
Seriously?

557
00:34:48.336 --> 00:34:51.756
You'd think they'd know better
than to just leave this shit lying around.

558
00:34:51.839 --> 00:34:54.679
Except then they'd know better
than to take pictures in the first place.

559
00:35:00.014 --> 00:35:01.014
Shit.

560
00:35:02.850 --> 00:35:05.490
- What are you doing in here?
- [Clay] We know about the Clubhouse.

561
00:35:05.561 --> 00:35:07.289
We know everything.
and we're not the only ones.

562
00:35:07.313 --> 00:35:09.273
Oh. you know everything? I don't think so.

563
00:35:09.565 --> 00:35:10.566
We know enough.

564
00:35:10.650 --> 00:35:14.487
- Hey. just back off. Dempsey.
- Or what. Justin?

565
00:35:15.071 --> 00:35:16.071
Gonna come at me?

566
00:35:16.322 --> 00:35:18.282
I wasn't scared of you
even before you fell apart.

567
00:35:18.783 --> 00:35:19.867
Do what you want. Zach.

568
00:35:19.951 --> 00:35:21.970
I've had the shit beat out of me
once this week already.

569
00:35:21.994 --> 00:35:23.496
It's not gonna stop us.

570
00:35:24.038 --> 00:35:25.123
- Really?
- Yes.

571
00:35:25.206 --> 00:35:26.874
'Cause it's gonna keep happening. Clay.

572
00:35:28.167 --> 00:35:30.461
To you. too. Justin. It doesn't stop.

573
00:35:30.795 --> 00:35:33.275
You can't take shots at the top
and expect to not get hit back.

574
00:35:35.633 --> 00:35:36.633
I'm not afraid.

575
00:35:39.303 --> 00:35:40.303
Good.

576
00:35:45.643 --> 00:35:47.061
You already have three of these.

577
00:35:50.064 --> 00:35:51.274
There's the rest.

578
00:35:52.692 --> 00:35:53.693
Wait. wait.

579
00:35:55.695 --> 00:35:59.073
It was you? Why the big mystery?
Why couldn't you just talk to me?

580
00:35:59.157 --> 00:36:01.477
- Tell me what was going on?
- 'Cause I'm a fucking coward.

581
00:36:03.995 --> 00:36:04.995
And you're not.

582
00:36:10.585 --> 00:36:13.337
[Tony] I try to do right by my friends.
to be strong.

583
00:36:13.754 --> 00:36:14.754
[door closes]

584
00:36:19.677 --> 00:36:21.804
To be true... like Hannah.

585
00:36:24.640 --> 00:36:27.018
[door unlocks. opens]

586
00:36:27.476 --> 00:36:28.476
Sorry!

587
00:36:29.228 --> 00:36:30.228
[door shuts]

588
00:36:30.438 --> 00:36:31.438
Phil...

589
00:36:32.648 --> 00:36:34.734
mixed up two prescriptions.

590
00:36:34.817 --> 00:36:38.279
Well. nearly. It was a disaster. It...

591
00:36:40.865 --> 00:36:41.865
Jackie?

592
00:37:01.969 --> 00:37:03.346
[sighs]

593
00:37:24.700 --> 00:37:27.245
[Tony] But sometimes a friendship
can't take the truth.

594
00:37:30.665 --> 00:37:33.292
So you find yourself
trying to be someone you're not.

595
00:37:34.835 --> 00:37:37.171
- [voices overlapping]
- [faint music playing]

596
00:37:47.181 --> 00:37:48.181
Sorry.

597
00:37:49.725 --> 00:37:50.725
Sorry.

598
00:37:51.727 --> 00:37:52.727
Excuse me.

599
00:37:53.396 --> 00:37:54.939
Just... very sorry.

600
00:37:56.816 --> 00:38:00.111
Asshole! You're just in time.
The set's about to start.

601
00:38:00.194 --> 00:38:02.446
Should we try and find a spot
closer to the stage?

602
00:38:02.530 --> 00:38:04.490
Yeah. let's go.
The boys are already up there.

603
00:38:04.573 --> 00:38:06.492
- We should get going.
- You never...

604
00:38:08.661 --> 00:38:09.861
I mean. they're all here. too?

605
00:38:09.996 --> 00:38:12.790
Of course. They're not gonna miss
a good show. Let's go. come on!

606
00:38:12.873 --> 00:38:13.913
All right. coming through.

607
00:38:14.542 --> 00:38:16.669
- [Cyrus] Move. move. move.
- Sorry.

608
00:38:16.919 --> 00:38:19.088
- Hey!
- What's up? You made it.

609
00:38:19.964 --> 00:38:21.684
- You all ready?
- Yeah! Let's do this shit.

610
00:38:21.716 --> 00:38:23.843
- All right! Here we go again.
- [crowd cheering]

611
00:38:25.052 --> 00:38:25.928
Get the party started.

612
00:38:26.012 --> 00:38:28.014
[playing punk metal music]

613
00:38:37.606 --> 00:38:39.859
[screaming lyrics]

614
00:39:13.267 --> 00:39:15.353
[cheering]

615
00:39:28.532 --> 00:39:31.243
[music continues]

616
00:40:04.902 --> 00:40:06.362
It's rough out there tonight. huh?

617
00:40:06.654 --> 00:40:08.572
- Oh. my God. are you okay?
- I'm fine.

618
00:40:10.324 --> 00:40:12.618
Okay. Can we talk?

619
00:40:12.701 --> 00:40:16.080
Because you've been avoiding me
for. like. two days straight.

620
00:40:16.163 --> 00:40:18.374
- No. I wasn't. I mean. I...
- No. it's okay.

621
00:40:18.999 --> 00:40:21.377
Look. I know what happened at the movies.

622
00:40:21.460 --> 00:40:24.064
- I don't know what you think happened...
- Don't have to be embarrassed.

623
00:40:24.088 --> 00:40:26.632
I even read that it's totally normal.
It's not even a thing.

624
00:40:26.715 --> 00:40:29.385
- Seriously. it happens...
- I know. but just shut up!

625
00:40:33.514 --> 00:40:34.640
Okay? Look. I...

626
00:40:36.058 --> 00:40:39.186
I don't know what you think happened.
but I left because you're fucking...

627
00:40:40.438 --> 00:40:44.567
boring and...
'cause I don't like you like that.

628
00:40:47.027 --> 00:40:49.363
What the fuck? Tyler?

629
00:40:50.990 --> 00:40:52.074
Okay. wait. No. hold on.

630
00:40:52.158 --> 00:40:54.201
Cyrus. just let...
No. let me explain real quick...

631
00:40:54.285 --> 00:40:57.121
No one fucking talks to my sister
like that.

632
00:41:00.291 --> 00:41:01.333
Get the fuck out.

633
00:41:03.461 --> 00:41:05.463
Get the fuck out!

634
00:41:05.546 --> 00:41:07.381
- [stammers]
- Go!

635
00:41:09.091 --> 00:41:10.091
Go!

636
00:41:12.553 --> 00:41:13.554
Get the fuck out!

637
00:41:20.853 --> 00:41:22.438
You must think I'm pretty messed up

638
00:41:23.439 --> 00:41:25.941
after hearing all that stuff
about me today. about my past.

639
00:41:27.610 --> 00:41:29.653
Obviously. it's not anything I'm proud of.

640
00:41:29.737 --> 00:41:32.072
Tony. we've all done things
we're not proud of.

641
00:41:34.825 --> 00:41:37.119
And they seem to find out
about the one thing...

642
00:41:40.581 --> 00:41:41.624
you wish they wouldn't.

643
00:41:44.210 --> 00:41:45.377
Actually. they didn't.

644
00:41:48.547 --> 00:41:51.300
Hannah didn't trust me with the tapes
because we were friends.

645
00:41:52.968 --> 00:41:54.887
She trusted me because I owed her.

646
00:41:59.642 --> 00:42:01.185
- Hannah...
- Shit. Tony. are you okay?

647
00:42:01.268 --> 00:42:03.229
I did something stupid.
The cops are coming.

648
00:42:03.521 --> 00:42:04.980
What? Why? What happened?

649
00:42:05.064 --> 00:42:07.191
Look. I can't get busted again.
I could get locked up.

650
00:42:07.274 --> 00:42:08.651
Please hide me.

651
00:42:10.152 --> 00:42:10.986
There's no time!

652
00:42:11.070 --> 00:42:12.947
[distant siren wails]

653
00:42:13.239 --> 00:42:14.532
Oh. shit. okay... uh...

654
00:42:15.616 --> 00:42:17.451
Go down the hall to the back office.

655
00:42:17.535 --> 00:42:18.577
I'll take care of it. Go!

656
00:42:18.661 --> 00:42:19.912
[siren chirps]

657
00:42:24.875 --> 00:42:25.875
Can I help you?

658
00:42:26.627 --> 00:42:28.212
Miss. we're responding to an assault.

659
00:42:29.088 --> 00:42:31.048
Oh. my God. An assault?

660
00:42:31.131 --> 00:42:33.884
Yeah. suspect is a Hispanic male.
late teens or early 20s.

661
00:42:33.968 --> 00:42:36.804
last seen fleeing on foot in the area.
wearing a black leather jacket.

662
00:42:37.179 --> 00:42:39.682
Have you seen anyone come in here
matching that description?

663
00:42:41.392 --> 00:42:42.685
No. No. I haven't.

664
00:42:44.436 --> 00:42:45.604
All right. [sighs]

665
00:42:49.275 --> 00:42:52.152
[door opens. shuts]

666
00:42:56.532 --> 00:43:00.369
I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to drag you into this.

667
00:43:03.914 --> 00:43:05.374
I went too far. I know I did.

668
00:43:08.919 --> 00:43:12.047
I know you think I'm this sweet.
nice girl. but...

669
00:43:13.757 --> 00:43:15.759
I was an asshole to someone
at my old school.

670
00:43:17.678 --> 00:43:20.639
I was trying to fit in with these girls.
and they were ganging up on her.

671
00:43:20.723 --> 00:43:23.434
And I thought. better to be
one of them than to be her.

672
00:43:24.810 --> 00:43:26.228
So. what ended up happening?

673
00:43:27.563 --> 00:43:31.358
A bunch of stuff went down.
and. uh... now I'm here.

674
00:43:36.030 --> 00:43:38.240
I just... I wish I could take it all back.

675
00:43:38.866 --> 00:43:39.866
You know?

676
00:43:46.957 --> 00:43:50.085
Hannah was a friend to me
and she kept my secrets.

677
00:43:50.669 --> 00:43:52.504
I wanted to do the same for her today.

678
00:43:54.256 --> 00:43:55.256
Thank you...

679
00:43:55.924 --> 00:43:58.093
for telling me that.

680
00:44:01.430 --> 00:44:03.599
I'm glad to know
that Hannah kept your secret.

681
00:44:05.559 --> 00:44:10.230
And I understand why she wanted
to protect you. I just...

682
00:44:11.899 --> 00:44:17.154
I wish I could've done that
for you today in court.

683
00:44:17.237 --> 00:44:20.157
No. it's my record. That's on me.

684
00:44:21.950 --> 00:44:22.950
Not you.

685
00:44:26.538 --> 00:44:29.333
[sighs] I guess we're all carrying
stuff around. right?

686
00:44:39.635 --> 00:44:40.635
What?

687
00:44:41.679 --> 00:44:42.763
[pings]

688
00:44:43.847 --> 00:44:44.932
No. you didn't.

689
00:44:48.310 --> 00:44:49.687
Fucking Marcus.

690
00:44:51.730 --> 00:44:53.232
Tyler. we need to talk.

691
00:44:53.816 --> 00:44:54.900
What happened to you?

692
00:44:55.776 --> 00:44:58.737
Nothing. I was at a concert with Cyrus.

693
00:44:59.196 --> 00:45:00.196
Uh. I'm fine.

694
00:45:01.198 --> 00:45:04.243
Listen. Tyler. Marcus Cole's father
was here a little while ago.

695
00:45:04.493 --> 00:45:07.955
He says that you and Cyrus
are blackmailing Marcus online?

696
00:45:08.747 --> 00:45:13.794
Okay. you guys. Marcus is a liar
and a creep. okay?

697
00:45:14.002 --> 00:45:17.923
He goes around and acts like this
great guy. but he treats girls like crap.

698
00:45:18.006 --> 00:45:21.135
- Did you hear what was on his tape?
- Whatever Marcus did is beside the point.

699
00:45:21.260 --> 00:45:24.012
If you have a problem with someone.
you tell us or a teacher.

700
00:45:24.096 --> 00:45:26.223
You don't just go around
trying to settle the score.

701
00:45:26.306 --> 00:45:28.559
Honey. it's just not like you
to do something like this.

702
00:45:29.059 --> 00:45:30.894
Did Cyrus pressure you into doing this?

703
00:45:33.772 --> 00:45:34.772
He...

704
00:45:37.109 --> 00:45:38.861
He said it would teach Marcus a lesson.

705
00:45:40.070 --> 00:45:42.239
I don't want you spending time
with him anymore.

706
00:45:42.322 --> 00:45:44.366
Okay! Fine! Whatever. I won't.

707
00:45:44.450 --> 00:45:47.286
Good. But that doesn't mean
you don't still have consequences.

708
00:45:47.369 --> 00:45:49.788
We're gonna confiscate
all your electronics.

709
00:45:49.872 --> 00:45:50.873
starting with your phone.

710
00:45:51.790 --> 00:45:53.500
Okay? This behavior stops now.

711
00:45:55.502 --> 00:45:56.503
Okay.

712
00:45:57.713 --> 00:45:58.713
And your cameras.

713
00:45:59.631 --> 00:46:02.342
No. Please... Mom...

714
00:46:03.343 --> 00:46:04.344
[Mr. Down] Sorry. Tyler.

715
00:46:06.221 --> 00:46:07.221
But. I...

716
00:46:16.690 --> 00:46:19.318
Hi. I don't know if you know who I am...

717
00:46:19.401 --> 00:46:20.401
No. I know who you are.

718
00:46:21.862 --> 00:46:23.322
I understand your anger.

719
00:46:25.157 --> 00:46:26.157
I do.

720
00:46:27.493 --> 00:46:29.328
I know you wanted
to get on that stand today

721
00:46:29.411 --> 00:46:31.330
and tell everyone
who you thought Hannah was.

722
00:46:32.623 --> 00:46:35.167
So did I. but I failed.

723
00:46:38.045 --> 00:46:39.245
And I'm here to make it right.

724
00:46:43.217 --> 00:46:44.426
She was a good person.

725
00:46:45.761 --> 00:46:46.970
She was a great friend.

726
00:46:49.556 --> 00:46:51.596
And what she did to you.
there's no excuse for that.

727
00:46:52.935 --> 00:46:54.186
I know she hurt you.

728
00:46:56.813 --> 00:46:57.856
She knew it. too.

729
00:47:00.192 --> 00:47:02.069
Now. I'm not asking you to forgive her.

730
00:47:03.737 --> 00:47:05.137
but you need to know she was sorry.

731
00:47:08.200 --> 00:47:10.536
She told me how sorry she felt.

732
00:47:23.298 --> 00:47:24.883
[faint buzzing]

733
00:47:27.135 --> 00:47:28.554
[buzzing]

734
00:47:29.513 --> 00:47:30.513
Hello.

735
00:47:31.974 --> 00:47:32.974
This is she.

736
00:47:36.562 --> 00:47:37.562
Oh. my God.

737
00:47:50.909 --> 00:47:51.909
Hi.

